       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg/day). Even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and gastrointestinal toxicity.\n\nThis may be a transcription error. Common intended regimens include 500 mg, 850 mg, or 1000 mg per dose, with a maximum of 1000 mg twice daily for immediate-release or 2000 mg once daily for extended-release.\n\nBecause you're not the prescriber, please have the ordering clinician confirm the intended dose, frequency, and formulation directly. Once they confirm, I can enter the corrected order, or you can enter it yourself if you're authorized to. If the 1700 mg dose was already entered elsewhere, please ask pharmacy to review it now."
